# Git change management

Detail: skill `git-change-management`. Snapshot: `docs/AGENT_DEVELOPMENT.md`
§ Workspace snapshot.

## Local commits (no owner approval)

The agent **may and should** create local commits on any local branch (including
`main`) at any time during modifying work — checkpoints, WIP, and completed chunks
— **without** waiting for operator approval.

- Prefer small coherent commits after validation (`run_dev_loop.py` / `--commit-gate`)
- Do not hide unfinished work in persistent `git stash`; use normal local commits
  (or a named branch + WIP commit) instead

## Commit shape (required)

- One concern per commit (product vs tooling vs agent-config vs docs-only)
- Subject: imperative mood, present tense, ~50–72 chars, ends with `.`
- Blank line between subject and body when a body is present
- Subject says **why** / user-visible outcome — not a file list
- Optional body: 1–3 lines of why/context; no bullet dumps of paths
- Do **not** use Conventional Commit type prefixes (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`)
- Do **not** use wave/phase labels in the subject (`Wave E:`, `Phase 10:`)
- Do **not** create empty “sync tracker to tip HEAD” commits; fold evidence notes
  into the commit that produced the evidence

## Still owner-gated

- No `git push`, force-push, tag, GitHub Release, or package publish without an
  explicit owner request
- Never force-push `main` / `master`
- Never stage personal wordlists, local `spell-sync.toml`, credentials, or
  maintainer home paths
- No history rewrite (`reset --hard`, `clean -fd`, rebase rewrite) without an
  explicit owner request

## Before a local commit

1. `python3 scripts/agent_context.py` (optional `--json`) then `git status` / `git diff`.
2. Validation appropriate to the boundary (edit loop or `--commit-gate`).
3. Subject + optional body per **Commit shape** above.

## Project note (vs nix-darwin)

Local commits anywhere are allowed here without operator approval. Remote push
remains owner-gated.
